# The Docker build context is the repo root (uv workspace builds need every
# member present to match uv.lock), so `COPY . .` would otherwise send the whole
# tree to the daemon. Two reasons to trim it:
#   1. Size/speed — keep .venv, caches, and other generated artifacts out of the
#      context so the transfer and build stay fast. (The builder runs its own
#      `uv sync` into a fresh image venv, so nothing here is about the host
#      .venv "clobbering" the image — it can't; this is purely context weight.)
#   2. Hygiene — never ship .git history or secrets (.env) into the build
#      context / daemon.
.git
.github
.venv
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.mypy_cache
**/.mypy_cache
.pytest_cache
**/.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
**/.ruff_cache
.env
**/.env
htmlcov
**/*.egg-info
deploy/compose
# Exclude docs from the build context, EXCEPT the runbook corpus — the
# knowledge-service image bakes it in for the indexer (see its Dockerfile).
docs/*
!docs/runbooks
